# The CallbackWriteFileRecord function is a callback function that a user implements and
# registers with
# the CAS BACnet Stack to write record-access files. This callback is called when the CAS BACnet
# Stack
# receives an AtomicWriteFileRequest BACnet message naming a File object whose
# File_Access_Method is
# record access (ASHRAE 135 cl. 14.2).
#
# Records arrive as one contiguous payload buffer plus a parallel array of per-record lengths,
# the same
# framing #CASBACnetStack::FPCallbackReadFileRecord uses.
#
# Per cl. 14.2.5, writing at a 'fileStartRecord' beyond the current Record_Count extends the
# file to
# that size; the contents of any intervening records are a local matter.
#
