def BACnetStack_AddFileObject(
    deviceInstance,
    objectInstance,
    isWritable,
    isConfigurationFile,
    fileAccessMethod,
):
    """Adds a File Object. The device must be added first before this function can be called.
    The only File properties that are handled and stored by the CAS BACnet Stack are:
    - FileAccessMethod (set by this function)
    - PropertyList

    Callbacks are used to handle other properties. The following list contains the required
    properties
    and the Callbacks that are used to get the required data:

    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Property Datatype Callback
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ObjectName CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
    FileType CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
    FileSize Unsigned CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
    CallbackSetPropertyUnsignedInteger (if writable)
    ModificationDate BACnetDateTime CallbackGetPropertyDate
    CallbackGetPropertyTime
    Archive Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
    CallbackSetPropertyBool
    ReadOnly Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
    RecordCount* Unsigned CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
    Only if FileAccessMethod is set to RecordAccess
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Calling this function again for a File Object that already exists updates the property
    set to match the
    fileAccessMethod given on the later call:
    - RecordCount is added or removed. ASHRAE 135-2024 Table 12-16 footnote 2 requires this:
    the
    property "shall be present only if File_Access_Method is RECORD_ACCESS".
    - FileSize is made writable for a writable stream-access file and non-writable
    otherwise. Only the
    first half is required (footnote 1: "If the file size can be changed by writing to the
    file, and
    File_Access_Method is STREAM_ACCESS, then this property shall be writable" - a
    sufficient
    condition, not a prohibition). Withholding a writable FileSize from a record-access file
    is a
    CAS BACnet Stack policy decision: cl. 12.13.6 defines writing FileSize in octets, which
    has no
    defined meaning against record boundaries, and a record file resizes through
    RecordCount.
    - The isConfigurationFile listing is add-only: a repeat call will not list the same
    object twice,
    but it also will not remove an object from ConfigurationFiles that an earlier call
    added.

    DECLARED LIMIT for record access - at most 128 records per AtomicReadFile request, and
    at most 2048
    octets of record data. This is a deliberate bound (stack-allocated buffers, embedded
    targets) and it
    is a declared deviation from ASHRAE 135-2024 cl. 14.1.5, so it must be declared in the
    PICS/EPICS of a
    product built on this stack. See #BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackReadFileRecord for the
    full statement.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_AddFileObject(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const
    uint32_t objectInstance, const bool isWritable, const bool isConfigurationFile, const
    uint8_t fileAccessMethod)

    Args:
        deviceInstance: (in) The instance number of the device that owns this File Object. [const
            uint32_t deviceInstance]
        objectInstance: (in) The instance number of this File Object. [const uint32_t objectInstance]
        isWritable: (in) A flag that determines if the file is writable. This sets the File's
            ReadOnly property flag to true (if not writable) or false. If writable, the
            File's FileSize property is made writable. The CAS BACnet Stack supports only
            writing a value of 0 to the FileSize property which should delete all the
            contents of the file but not the file itself. [const bool isWritable]
        isConfigurationFile: (in) A flag that determines if the file is a configuration file. Configuration
            files do not increment the DatabaseRevision property when they are added or
            removed. [const bool isConfigurationFile]
        fileAccessMethod: (in) The File_Access_Method of this File Object: Record Access = 0, Stream
            Access = 1. Any other value is rejected. Record-access File objects are served
            by the callbacks registered with #BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackReadFileRecord /
            #BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackWriteFileRecord, and their RecordCount property is
            enabled automatically. See the repeat-call and record-limit notes above. [const
            uint8_t fileAccessMethod]

    Returns:
        True on success; false if the device does not exist, the object could not be
        added, File-object support was not compiled, or one of the object's stored
        properties could not be saved. IMPORTANT for that last case: the File object may
        ALREADY be present in Object_List even though false was returned, missing
        File_Access_Method and/or File_Read_Only - which makes every
        AtomicReadFile/AtomicWriteFile against it fail. Read false as "this object is
        not usable" rather than "nothing happened", and remove the object or restart
        configuration.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_AddFileObject(
        deviceInstance,
        objectInstance,
        isWritable,
        isConfigurationFile,
        fileAccessMethod,
    )


