def BACnetStack_AddEventLogObject(deviceInstance, objectInstance, maxBufferSize):
    """Adds a BACnet Event Log Object. The device must be added first.
    Records normally accumulate from received event notifications. For test purposes,
    records can be
    seeded via the test-tool-only BACnetStack_InsertEventLogRecord
    (CASBACnetStackTestToolDLL.h), which
    advances Total_Record_Count (the monitored property for the BUFFER_READY event
    algorithm).

    The Event Log properties that are handled and stored by the CAS BACnet Stack are:
    - Enable, Stop_When_Full
    - Buffer_Size, Record_Count, Total_Record_Count
    - Notification_Threshold, Records_Since_Notification, Last_Notify_Record
    - Log_Buffer, Object_Identifier, Object_Type, Status_Flags, Property_List
    These are answered from stack storage BEFORE any callback is consulted, so a registered
    Get
    callback CANNOT override them, and writes to the writable ones land in the same storage
    rather
    than in a Set callback.
    Start_Time and Stop_Time are also stored by the stack, but this function does NOT enable
    them
    (they are optional in cl. 12.27). Until BACnetStack_SetPropertyEnabled is called for
    them, a
    read returns Error(PROPERTY, UNKNOWN_PROPERTY).
    Once intrinsic BUFFER_READY reporting is enabled, Notification_Threshold,
    Records_Since_Notification and Last_Notify_Record are served by the event algorithm
    instead of
    by this object's own members, for both reads and writes.
    Log_Buffer records are retrieved with ReadRange. KNOWN ISSUE: unlike the Trend Log, a
    ReadProperty of Event Log Log_Buffer is not refused - it answers with an EMPTY list and
    a
    success status. Do not read Log_Buffer with ReadProperty.

    Callbacks are used to handle the remaining required properties. The following list
    contains
    those properties and the Callbacks that are used to get the required data:

    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Property Datatype Callback
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ObjectName CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
    CallbackSetPropertyCharacterString
    (only if made writable)
    EventState* Enumerated CallbackGetPropertyEnumerated
    Served by the stack's intrinsic alarm engine instead, if intrinsic reporting has been
    enabled for this object. With neither an alarm engine nor a callback the stack
    answers NORMAL.
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_AddEventLogObject(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const
    uint32_t objectInstance, const uint32_t maxBufferSize)

    Args:
        deviceInstance: (in) The instance of the device that the event log object is added to. [const
            uint32_t deviceInstance]
        objectInstance: (in) The instance of the event log object being added. [const uint32_t
            objectInstance]
        maxBufferSize: (in) The maximum number of records to maintain in memory. [const uint32_t
            maxBufferSize]

    Returns:
        Returns true if successful, false if failed.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_AddEventLogObject(deviceInstance, objectInstance, maxBufferSize)


def BACnetStack_AddChannelObject(deviceInstance, channelObjectInstance, presentValueDatatype):
    """Configures a Channel object's stack-held data: the concrete primitive datatype of its
    Present_Value
    (a BACnetChannelValue CHOICE) and an initially-empty List_Of_Object_Property_References.

    TRAP: the datatype is FIXED here, at configuration time. 135-2024 cl. 12.53.5 defines
    Present_Value as whatever was most recently written to it, so a Channel whose clients
    write more
    than one datatype cannot be modelled through this export - the stored code is what the
    stack uses
    to dispatch every Present_Value read to a typed Get callback.

    The only Channel properties that are handled and stored by the CAS BACnet Stack are:
    - ObjectIdentifier, ObjectType, PropertyList, StatusFlags
    - the PresentValue BACnetChannelValue CHOICE selector (set by presentValueDatatype),
    which the
    stack uses to pick the typed callbacks below
    - ListOfObjectPropertyReferences (maintained by
    BACnetStack_AddObjectPropertyReferenceToChannel, writable in place by a client
    WriteProperty, and used by the stack to fan a WriteGroup out to the referenced
    properties)
    - ExecutionDelay (#967: also maintained by
    BACnetStack_AddObjectPropertyReferenceToChannel,
    appended in lockstep with each reference so it can never disagree in length with
    ListOfObjectPropertyReferences - see that function's doc. A client WriteProperty
    replaces the
    whole array and is rejected if the new length does not match
    ListOfObjectPropertyReferences.)

    Everything else is served by the application - including ChannelNumber and
    ControlGroups, which are
    required and writable:

    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Property Datatype Callback
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ObjectName CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
    PresentValue BACnetChannelValue CallbackGetPropertyBool (the NULL-slot flag)
    CallbackGetProperty<T>, T = presentValueDatatype
    CallbackSetProperty<T> / CallbackSetPropertyNull
    All of these are called with
    propertyIdentifier = PriorityArray,
    useArrayIndex = true, index 1..16.
    LastPriority Unsigned CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
    WriteStatus Enumerated CallbackGetPropertyEnumerated
    OutOfService Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
    ChannelNumber Unsigned16 CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
    CallbackSetPropertyUnsignedInteger
    ControlGroups Unsigned32 array CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
    CallbackSetPropertyUnsignedInteger
    Array index 0 is the element count.
    AllowGroupDelayInhibit*
    Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
    Optional; enable it with BACnetStack_SetPropertyEnabled first.
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    IMPORTANT: the WriteGroup service reads ChannelNumber and ControlGroups back through the
    callbacks
    above (ControlGroups at array index 0 for the count, then 1..N). An application that
    does not
    serve them reports channel number 0 and an empty ControlGroups, and the Channel then
    never matches
    a WriteGroup request.

    IMPORTANT: a PresentValue read whose 16 priority slots are all NULL falls back to a
    RelinquishDefault read - and RelinquishDefault is not a Channel property, so that read
    returns
    Error(PROPERTY, UNKNOWN_PROPERTY). Serve at least one priority slot.

    KNOWN ISSUE: ListOfObjectPropertyReferences is missing from the object's PropertyList,
    although
    the property itself reads correctly. A conformance tester that reads PropertyList and
    then reads
    each entry will not see it.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_AddChannelObject(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const
    uint32_t channelObjectInstance, const uint8_t presentValueDatatype)

    Args:
        deviceInstance: (in) The device instance that owns this Channel object. [const uint32_t
            deviceInstance]
        channelObjectInstance: (in) The Channel object's instance. Add the BACnet object itself separately with
            BACnetStack_AddObject: this call neither creates it nor checks that it exists,
            so a typo here silently creates stack data for an object that is not there and
            fails at read time. Calling this again for the same instance REPLACES the
            datatype without warning and keeps the existing
            List_Of_Object_Property_References. [const uint32_t channelObjectInstance]
        presentValueDatatype: (in) The primitive application datatype of Present_Value. Use a value from
            #CASBACnetStack::BACnetTagApplicationDatatypes (0 = Null through 12 =
            BACnetObjectIdentifier). NOT validated - any other value is stored and then
            matches no read dispatch, so Present_Value reads fail. The constructed
            BACnetChannelValue alternatives (lighting-command, xy-color, color-command)
            cannot be selected: they have no application tag. [const uint8_t
            presentValueDatatype]

    Returns:
        True on success; false if no device has been added, allocation fails, or Channel
        support is not compiled.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_AddChannelObject(
        deviceInstance,
        channelObjectInstance,
        presentValueDatatype,
    )


def BACnetStack_AddObjectPropertyReferenceToChannel(
    deviceInstance,
    channelObjectInstance,
    refObjectType,
    refObjectInstance,
    refPropertyIdentifier,
    refUsePropertyArrayIndex,
    refPropertyArrayIndex,
    refUseDeviceIdentifier,
    refDeviceInstance,
    executionDelay,
):
    """Appends one reference to a Channel object's stack-held
    List_Of_Object_Property_References, AND
    (#967) one delay to its stack-held Execution_Delay, in the same call.

    135-2024 cl. 12.53.11.2/.12.1 require List_Of_Object_Property_References and
    Execution_Delay to be
    the SAME LENGTH. Before #967, Execution_Delay was served entirely by the application's
    own property
    callbacks, with nothing coupling the two arrays - a caller that called this function N
    times without
    separately growing its own Execution_Delay callback to also report N elements shipped a
    Channel
    object whose two arrays disagreed in length, a conformance failure with no diagnostic.
    Execution_Delay
    is now held in the stack alongside List_Of_Object_Property_References, appended together
    here, so the
    two can never disagree.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_AddObjectPropertyReferenceToChannel(const uint32_t
    deviceInstance, const uint32_t channelObjectInstance, const uint16_t refObjectType,
    const uint32_t refObjectInstance, const uint32_t refPropertyIdentifier, const bool
    refUsePropertyArrayIndex, const uint32_t refPropertyArrayIndex, const bool
    refUseDeviceIdentifier, const uint32_t refDeviceInstance, const uint32_t executionDelay)

    Args:
        deviceInstance: (in) The device instance that owns this Channel object. [const uint32_t
            deviceInstance]
        channelObjectInstance: (in) The Channel object to modify. [const uint32_t channelObjectInstance]
        refObjectType: (in) The referenced object type. See #CASBACnetStack::BACnetObjectType. [const
            uint16_t refObjectType]
        refObjectInstance: (in) The referenced object instance. [const uint32_t refObjectInstance]
        refPropertyIdentifier: (in) The referenced property identifier. [const uint32_t refPropertyIdentifier]
        refUsePropertyArrayIndex: (in) True if the reference targets one array element of the property. [const
            bool refUsePropertyArrayIndex]
        refPropertyArrayIndex: (in) The array index, used only when refUsePropertyArrayIndex is true. [const
            uint32_t refPropertyArrayIndex]
        refUseDeviceIdentifier: (in) True if the reference names an explicit device (a remote target); false for
            a local object. [const bool refUseDeviceIdentifier]
        refDeviceInstance: (in) The device instance, used only when refUseDeviceIdentifier is true. SIDE
            EFFECT: when this names a device other than this one and other than 4194303,
            that device is added to the stack's Device Address Binding table, which starts
            ongoing background binding traffic for it. 4194303 is the spec's "empty
            reference" sentinel (135-2024 cl. 12.53.11.1). [const uint32_t
            refDeviceInstance]
        executionDelay: (in) The Execution_Delay value (seconds) for this reference; 0 means no delay.
            [const uint32_t executionDelay]

    Returns:
        True on success; false if no device has been added, BACnetStack_AddChannelObject
        has not been called for channelObjectInstance, allocation fails, or Channel
        support is not compiled. Each call APPENDS with no duplicate check and no upper
        bound, and there is no export to remove an entry; read the lists back with
        BACnetStack_SendReadProperty.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_AddObjectPropertyReferenceToChannel(
        deviceInstance,
        channelObjectInstance,
        refObjectType,
        refObjectInstance,
        refPropertyIdentifier,
        refUsePropertyArrayIndex,
        refPropertyArrayIndex,
        refUseDeviceIdentifier,
        refDeviceInstance,
        executionDelay,
    )


