def BACnetStack_RemoveGroupMember(
    deviceInstance,
    groupObjectInstance,
    memberObjectType,
    memberObjectInstance,
):
    """Removes one member from a Group object's stack-held List_Of_Group_Members. The companion
    to
    BACnetStack_AddGroupMember.

    Semantics match the RemoveListElement service on the same property, so the host API and
    the network
    agree about the same list:
    - The member is identified by its object identifier alone; ALL of its property
    references go with
    it - there is no per-property removal here, so this is only sufficient when you want the
    member
    gone entirely, not when you want to drop one of several properties
    BACnetStack_AddGroupMember
    appended to it.
    - Removing a member that is not in the list FAILS and returns false. This is
    deliberately not
    idempotent - RemoveListElement answers listElementNotFound for the same request.
    - The surviving members keep their order. ASHRAE 135-2024 cl. 12.14.5 does not mandate
    an order, but
    a client that reads the list, removes an entry and re-reads it would otherwise see the
    remainder
    shift.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_RemoveGroupMember(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const
    uint32_t groupObjectInstance, const uint16_t memberObjectType, const uint32_t
    memberObjectInstance)

    Args:
        deviceInstance: (in) The device instance that owns this Group object. [const uint32_t
            deviceInstance]
        groupObjectInstance: (in) The Group object to remove the member from. [const uint32_t
            groupObjectInstance]
        memberObjectType: (in) The member object type. See #CASBACnetStack::BACnetObjectType. [const
            uint16_t memberObjectType]
        memberObjectInstance: (in) The member object instance. [const uint32_t memberObjectInstance]

    Returns:
        True when a member was removed; false if the device or the Group object does not
        exist, the member is not in the list, or Group support is not compiled.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_RemoveGroupMember(
        deviceInstance,
        groupObjectInstance,
        memberObjectType,
        memberObjectInstance,
    )


