def BACnetStack_SetAlarmsAndEventsForObjectEnabled(
    deviceInstance,
    objectType,
    objectInstance,
    notificationClassInstance,
    notifyType,
    enableToOffNormalEvent,
    enableToFaultEvent,
    enableToNormalEvent,
    enableEventDetection,
    enabled,
):
    """Enables Alarms and Events for a specific object. The object and the notification class
    object must
    exist before calling this function, otherwise the function will return false.

    This function will enable the required properties and store the initial values in
    memory.

    NOTE: this function makes Event_Algorithm_Inhibit and Reliability_Evaluation_Inhibit
    WRITABLE, so
    a remote client can inhibit the algorithms armed by the SetIntrinsic* / SetFault*
    setters.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_SetAlarmsAndEventsForObjectEnabled(const uint32_t
    deviceInstance, const uint16_t objectType, const uint32_t objectInstance, const uint32_t
    notificationClassInstance, const uint8_t notifyType, const bool enableToOffNormalEvent,
    const bool enableToFaultEvent, const bool enableToNormalEvent, const bool
    enableEventDetection, const bool enabled)

    Args:
        deviceInstance: (in) The instance number of the device that owns this object. [const uint32_t
            deviceInstance]
        objectType: (in) The object type of the object for alarms and events. [const uint16_t
            objectType]
        objectInstance: (in) The object instance of the object for alarms and events. [const uint32_t
            objectInstance]
        notificationClassInstance: (in) The instance number of the notification class object that will handle the
            event notifications generated by this object. [const uint32_t
            notificationClassInstance]
        notifyType: (in) The type of notifications that this object generates. 0 = Alarm, 1 = Event.
            [const uint8_t notifyType]
        enableToOffNormalEvent: (in) Whether the To_OffNormal event is enabled (true) or not (false).
            Recommended value: true. [const bool enableToOffNormalEvent]
        enableToFaultEvent: (in) Whether the To_Fault event is enabled (true) or not (false). Recommended
            value: true. [const bool enableToFaultEvent]
        enableToNormalEvent: (in) Whether the To_Normal event is enabled (true) or not (false). Recommended
            value: true. [const bool enableToNormalEvent]
        enableEventDetection: (in) Whether event detection is enabled (true) or not (false). Recommended
            value: true [const bool enableEventDetection]
        enabled: (in) Master switch. TRAP: false is DESTRUCTIVE, not merely "skip". It FREES this
            object's alarm-and-event state - discarding any event or fault algorithm already
            armed by the BACnetStack_SetIntrinsic* / BACnetStack_SetFault* setters - and
            disables Event_State, Notification_Class, Event_Enable, Acked_Transitions,
            Notify_Type, Event_Time_Stamps, Event_Detection_Enable, Event_Algorithm_Inhibit
            and Reliability_Evaluation_Inhibit, then returns true. The other parameters are
            ignored when false. Re-enabling requires re-arming every algorithm from scratch.
            Recommended value: true. [const bool enabled]

    Returns:
        True on success; false if the device or object does not exist, if enabled is
        true and the Notification Class object does not exist, or if Alarm-and-Event
        support was not compiled (STACK_OPTION_ALARMS_AND_EVENTS).
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_SetAlarmsAndEventsForObjectEnabled(
        deviceInstance,
        objectType,
        objectInstance,
        notificationClassInstance,
        notifyType,
        enableToOffNormalEvent,
        enableToFaultEvent,
        enableToNormalEvent,
        enableEventDetection,
        enabled,
    )


