def BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackReceiveMessageForPort(FPCallbackReceiveMessageForPort):
    """Registers the callback the stack calls to pull one inbound raw BACnet message from the
    host's
    transport layer. Called exactly once per BACnetStack_Tick(), and from nowhere else.

    MUST NOT BLOCK-WAIT. Tick() cannot proceed until this returns. Return 0 when no message
    is
    waiting; that is the normal idle case, not an error.

    The callback returns the number of bytes it wrote into the message buffer. The stack
    DISCARDS the
    whole message, and logs, if that count exceeds maxMessageLength or if either
    connection-string
    length exceeds maxConnectionStringLength - it does not clamp.

    All four buffers belong to the stack, are its own call-frame locals, and are valid only
    for the
    duration of the call. Write into them; never retain them. The two length out-parameters
    are
    OUT-only - their values on entry are undefined.

    If this callback is never registered the stack reads nothing, reports no error, and the
    device is
    silently deaf.

    C declaration: void
    BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackReceiveMessageForPort(uint16_t(*FPCallbackReceiveMessageForPort)(uint8_t*
    message, const uint16_t maxMessageLength, uint8_t* sourceConnectionString, uint8_t*
    sourceConnectionStringLength, uint8_t* destinationConnectionString, uint8_t*
    destinationConnectionStringLength, const uint8_t maxConnectionStringLength, uint32_t*
    networkPortInstance))

    Args:
        FPCallbackReceiveMessageForPort: (in) The function pointer for the CallbackReceiveMessageForPort function. See
            #CASBACnetStack::FPCallbackReceiveMessageForPort for more info.
            [uint16_t(*FPCallbackReceiveMessageForPort)(uint8_t* message, const uint16_t
            maxMessageLength, uint8_t* sourceConnectionString, uint8_t*
            sourceConnectionStringLength, uint8_t* destinationConnectionString, uint8_t*
            destinationConnectionStringLength, const uint8_t maxConnectionStringLength,
            uint32_t* networkPortInstance)]
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackReceiveMessageForPort(FPCallbackReceiveMessageForPort)


def BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackSendMessageForPort(FPCallbackSendMessageForPort):
    """Registers the callback the stack calls to hand one outbound raw BACnet frame to the
    host's
    transport layer. Fires from inside BACnetStack_Tick() AND synchronously from every
    BACnetStack_Send* export before that export returns.

    THE RETURN IS A FLAG, NOT A COUNT. The stack only tests it against zero: 0 means "not
    sent" and
    fails the send, any non-zero value means success. It is never compared with
    messageLength, so a
    partial write reported honestly is still treated as a complete send. Return 0 or the
    full length;
    nothing else is meaningful.

    Both the message and the connection string are stack-owned and valid only for the
    duration of the
    call. The connection string is NULL with length 0 when the frame has no destination
    address -
    that means broadcast on this data link.

    If this callback is never registered the stack can answer nothing: each send site logs
    "CallbackSendMessageForPort does not exist" and drops the frame with no BACnet-level
    diagnostic.

    C declaration: void
    BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackSendMessageForPort(uint16_t(*FPCallbackSendMessageForPort)(const
    uint8_t* message, const uint16_t messageLength, const uint8_t* connectionString, const
    uint8_t connectionStringLength, const uint32_t networkPortInstance, bool broadcast))

    Args:
        FPCallbackSendMessageForPort: (in) The function pointer for the CallbackSendMessageForPort function. See
            #CASBACnetStack::FPCallbackSendMessageForPort for more info.
            [uint16_t(*FPCallbackSendMessageForPort)(const uint8_t* message, const uint16_t
            messageLength, const uint8_t* connectionString, const uint8_t
            connectionStringLength, const uint32_t networkPortInstance, bool broadcast)]
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackSendMessageForPort(FPCallbackSendMessageForPort)


