def BACnetStack_SendRegisterForeignDevice(
    networkPortInstance,
    timeToLive,
    connectionString,
    connectionStringLength,
):
    """Sends a RegisterForeignDevice BVLL message to a specified BBMD (BACnet Broadcast
    Management
    Device) to register as a foreign device on the BACnet IP network.

    PRECONDITION: BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackGetSystemTime must have been registered first;
    without a clock the time-to-live cannot be tracked and this returns false before
    sending.

    A FALSE RETURN DOES NOT ALWAYS MEAN NOTHING HAPPENED: if connectionStringLength is not
    exactly
    6 (BACnet/IP), the Register-Foreign-Device frame has ALREADY been transmitted and only
    the local
    record failed, so the BBMD may hold an FDT entry this device is not tracking.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_SendRegisterForeignDevice(const uint32_t
    networkPortInstance, const uint16_t timeToLive, const uint8_t* connectionString, const
    uint8_t connectionStringLength)

    Args:
        networkPortInstance: (in) The IPv4 Network Port object instance to send on. Sprint 199 Phase 3
            (#822/#556 Q4): new leading parameter - this whole BVLL/FD/BBMD family used to
            act on Network Port instance 0 implicitly, with no way to name a different one.
            [const uint32_t networkPortInstance]
        timeToLive: (in) The number of seconds within which this device must re-register with a BBMD
            or risk it being purged from the BBMD's Foreign Device Table. THE STACK DOES NOT
            AUTO-RENEW. It tracks the deadline locally and, when it passes, drops its own
            foreign-device state and resets the Network Port's BACnetIPMode to normal. The
            host must call this function again before the time-to-live expires. 0 is
            accepted but expires on the next tick, cancelling the registration locally while
            the BBMD may still hold the entry - it does NOT mean "forever". [const uint16_t
            timeToLive]
        connectionString: (in) The connection string that represents the IP Address and Port of the BBMD
            to send the RegisterForeignDevice message. Example: 0xC0, 0xA8, 0x01, 0x05,
            0xBA, 0xC0 is 192.168.1.5:47808. [const uint8_t* connectionString]
        connectionStringLength: (in) The number of bytes in the connection string. [const uint8_t
            connectionStringLength]

    Returns:
        True if successfully sent, otherwise false.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_SendRegisterForeignDevice(
        networkPortInstance,
        timeToLive,
        connectionString,
        connectionStringLength,
    )


