def BACnetStack_DeleteFDTEntry(index):
    """Deletes one entry from this device's foreign device table by index.

    The index is the SAME index space as BACnetStack_GetFDTEntry, and deleting shifts every
    later entry
    down by one. A loop that reads index N then deletes it will therefore SKIP the entry
    that moved
    into N. Delete from the highest index downwards, or re-enumerate from 0 after each
    delete.

    This function transmits nothing - the removed foreign device is not told, and keeps
    sending to this
    BBMD until its own re-registration attempt fails.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_DeleteFDTEntry(const uint16_t index)

    Args:
        index: (in) The zero-based table position to delete. [const uint16_t index]

    Returns:
        True if an entry existed at that index and was removed. False if the index is
        out of range, the IPv4 datalink or the BBMD does not exist, or BBMD support was
        not compiled.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_DeleteFDTEntry(index)


