def BACnetStack_SendUnsubscribedUnconfirmedCOVNotification(
    initiatingDeviceInstance,
    subscriberProcessIdentifier,
    monitoredObjectType,
    monitoredObjectInstance,
    timeRemaining,
    properties,
    propertyCount,
    propertiesLength,
    connectionString,
    connectionStringLength,
    networkPortInstance,
    broadcast,
    destinationNetwork,
    destinationAddress,
    destinationAddressLength,
):
    """Sends an unconfirmed COV notification unprompted by any subscription (cl. 13.1.1), used
    by a
    device to announce a value on its own initiative rather than in response to
    SubscribeCOV.

    #1013: clause 21.3.2's UnconfirmedCOVNotification-Request has FIVE required fields.
    Until now this
    export could only supply two of them meaningfully - subscriber-process-identifier and
    time-remaining were hardwired to 0, and list-of-values carried exactly one property with
    no array
    index, so the Present_Value + Status_Flags pair clause 13.1 expects a notification to
    carry could
    not be sent at all. All three are now parameters.

    VALUES COME FROM THIS DEVICE'S OWN DATABASE, not from the caller (#1013 action item 4,
    decided
    2026-09-08 - see the issue). `initiatingDeviceInstance` must name a device added with
    BACnetStack_AddDevice, and each property's value is read from it exactly as a
    ReadProperty would.
    A gateway announcing on behalf of a device it proxies models that device as a VIRTUAL
    device
    (BACnetStack_AddVirtualNetwork + BACnetStack_AddDeviceToVirtualNetwork) and announces
    from it -
    at which point the values are local and this rule holds. Supplying values through the
    call
    instead would need a datatype-plus-bytes encoding per property, a far larger surface,
    and would
    let a caller announce a value the device would not itself report.

    `properties` is `propertyCount` packed elements, little-endian, each a FIXED 9 BYTES -
    the same
    shape convention as BACnetStack_SendSubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple's `references`:

    -[0]---------*-[1..4]--------------*-[5..8]---------------*
    | uint8 flags | uint32 propertyId | uint32 arrayIndex |
    -------------*---------------------*----------------------*

    flags: bit0 = usePropertyArrayIndex (when clear, arrayIndex is ignored and the whole
    property is
    sent). Every element names a property of the SAME monitored object - the object
    identifier is
    already given by monitoredObjectType/monitoredObjectInstance.

    `propertiesLength` is the total byte length of `properties` and must be at least
    propertyCount * 9; a shorter buffer is DETECTED and rejected rather than over-read.
    `propertyCount` must be at least 1.

    Worked example - announce Present_Value, no array index:
    00 55 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 (9 bytes total)
    |fl| |propertyId ||arrayIndex |
    propertyCount = 1, propertiesLength = 9. (propertyIdentifier 85 = Present_Value.)

    NOTE, PARAMETER-ORDER: unlike its four SendCOVNotification siblings, `broadcast` sits
    after
    `networkPortInstance` here (#937). It is kept there because moving it would be a second
    ABI break for no
    behavioural gain.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_SendUnsubscribedUnconfirmedCOVNotification(const
    uint32_t initiatingDeviceInstance, const uint32_t subscriberProcessIdentifier, const
    uint16_t monitoredObjectType, const uint32_t monitoredObjectInstance, const uint32_t
    timeRemaining, const void* properties, const uint32_t propertyCount, const uint32_t
    propertiesLength, const uint8_t* connectionString, const uint8_t connectionStringLength,
    const uint32_t networkPortInstance, const bool broadcast, const uint16_t
    destinationNetwork, const uint8_t* destinationAddress, const uint8_t
    destinationAddressLength)

    Args:
        initiatingDeviceInstance: (in) The LOCAL device the notification is announced from. [const uint32_t
            initiatingDeviceInstance]
        subscriberProcessIdentifier: (in) Clause 21.3.2's subscriber-process-identifier. 0 is the conventional value
            for an unsubscribed notification, and is what this export used to send
            unconditionally. [const uint32_t subscriberProcessIdentifier]
        monitoredObjectType: (in) The object whose properties are announced. [const uint16_t
            monitoredObjectType]
        monitoredObjectInstance: (in) The object whose properties are announced. [const uint32_t
            monitoredObjectInstance]
        timeRemaining: (in) Clause 21.3.2's time-remaining, in seconds. 0 means "not applicable", which
            is correct for an unsubscribed notification and was the previous hardwired
            value. [const uint32_t timeRemaining]
        properties: (in) The packed property list described above. [const void* properties]
        propertyCount: (in) The packed property list described above. [const uint32_t propertyCount]
        propertiesLength: (in) The packed property list described above. [const uint32_t propertiesLength]
        connectionString: (in) The datalink address to send TO (the destination) - not the local address
            to send from. For IPv4 this is 6 bytes: 4 octets of IPv4 address followed by 2
            octets of port, big-endian (e.g. 0xC0,0xA8,0x01,0x05,0xBA,0xC0 =
            192.168.1.5:47808; see BACnetStack_SendRegisterForeignDevice for a worked
            example). MS/TP and BACnet/SC use a different connection-string shape; see their
            respective Set/Send exports. [const uint8_t* connectionString]
        connectionStringLength: (in) The datalink address to send TO (the destination) - not the local address
            to send from. For IPv4 this is 6 bytes: 4 octets of IPv4 address followed by 2
            octets of port, big-endian (e.g. 0xC0,0xA8,0x01,0x05,0xBA,0xC0 =
            192.168.1.5:47808; see BACnetStack_SendRegisterForeignDevice for a worked
            example). MS/TP and BACnet/SC use a different connection-string shape; see their
            respective Set/Send exports. [const uint8_t connectionStringLength]
        networkPortInstance: (in) The Network Port object instance to send the message on, or
            BACNET_NETWORK_PORT_DEFAULT (4194303) for the default/single port. [const
            uint32_t networkPortInstance]
        broadcast: (in) Whether to broadcast rather than send to a single destination. [const bool
            broadcast]
        destinationNetwork: (in) The destination. [const uint16_t destinationNetwork]
        destinationAddress: (in) The destination. [const uint8_t* destinationAddress]
        destinationAddressLength: (in) The destination. [const uint8_t destinationAddressLength]

    Returns:
        True on success; false if the device or object does not exist, the packed buffer
        is malformed or too short, any named property cannot be read from the local
        database, or COV notification support was not compiled.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_SendUnsubscribedUnconfirmedCOVNotification(
        initiatingDeviceInstance,
        subscriberProcessIdentifier,
        monitoredObjectType,
        monitoredObjectInstance,
        timeRemaining,
        properties,
        propertyCount,
        propertiesLength,
        connectionString,
        connectionStringLength,
        networkPortInstance,
        broadcast,
        destinationNetwork,
        destinationAddress,
        destinationAddressLength,
    )


