def BACnetStack_SetBACnetSCHelloCapabilities(helloCapabilities):
    """Sets the Capabilities octet this device advertises in the BACnet/SC Hello destination
    option of
    Connect-Request and Connect-Accept (135-2024 Annex AB).

    CHANGING THIS DROPS CONNECTIONS. If the new value differs from the current one, every
    accepted
    hub-function peer and the direct-connect peer are disconnected through
    CallbackDisconnectWebsocket
    so the new Hello is exchanged on reconnect. Setting the value it already has is a no-op
    and
    disconnects nothing.

    DEVICE-WIDE: applied to EVERY BACnet/SC data link instance, not only the port you may
    have in mind.
    There is no per-Network-Port variant and no read-back.

    C declaration: bool BACnetStack_SetBACnetSCHelloCapabilities(const uint8_t
    helloCapabilities)

    Args:
        helloCapabilities: (in) The Capabilities octet. Per 135-2024, bit 0 (0x01) is "identity relay" and
            bits 1-7 are reserved, shall be 0, and are ignored by the receiver. The stack
            advertises this byte verbatim without validating it, and does not itself act on
            the identity-relay bit - nor on a peer's. Pass 0 unless a hub or peer requires
            otherwise. [const uint8_t helloCapabilities]

    Returns:
        True if the value was applied to every BACnet/SC data link instance. False if
        any instance rejected it, if no BACnet/SC data link exists, or if the stack was
        built without STACK_OPTION_DATA_LINK_LAYER_SC.
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_SetBACnetSCHelloCapabilities(helloCapabilities)


