def BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackSCStartListening(FPCallbackSCStartListening):
    """Registers the callback the stack calls to ask the host to start ACCEPTING inbound
    WebSocket
    connections on a URI - the hub-function and direct-connect accept roles. Fires from
    inside Tick().

    MANDATORY FOR ANY ACCEPT ROLE. With hub-function or direct-connect accept enabled and
    this callback
    unregistered, the BACnet/SC data link logs "CallbackSCStartListening has not been
    registered" and
    refuses to run, so the device never listens.

    THE RETURN IS HONORED. The stack marks itself listening only when you return true, and
    retries on
    every subsequent Tick while you return false. Do not report success for a listener you
    did not open.

    The URI is stack-owned and NUL-terminated, valid only for the duration of the call; the
    length
    excludes the terminator. Registering has no effect if BACnet/SC was not compiled
    (STACK_OPTION_DATA_LINK_LAYER_SC).

    C declaration: void
    BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackSCStartListening(bool(*FPCallbackSCStartListening)(const
    char* websocketUri, const uint32_t websocketUriLength))

    Args:
        FPCallbackSCStartListening: (in) The function pointer for the CallbackSCStartListening function. See
            #CASBACnetStack::FPCallbackSCStartListening for more info.
            [bool(*FPCallbackSCStartListening)(const char* websocketUri, const uint32_t
            websocketUriLength)]
    """
    return _lib().BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackSCStartListening(FPCallbackSCStartListening)


